## INTEGRATION WITH GIT WORKFLOW

**This validation runs BEFORE the git commit command:**

```bash
# User requests: "commit this"
# AI agent workflow:

1. Check if committing from IDE (local environment)
   → If yes, run local pre-commit validation
   → If no (cloud agent), skip (hook will run on server)

2. Run pre-commit hook locally
   → Auto-fix issues
   → Re-stage fixes
   → Re-run until passes

3. Run CI checks locally
   → Auto-fix issues
   → Re-stage fixes
   → Re-run until passes

4. Run ShellCheck (if available)
   → Report issues
   → Auto-fix if possible

5. If all checks pass:
   → Execute: git commit -m "..."
   → Git hook will run (should pass since we pre-validated)

6. If checks fail after 3 retries:
   → Block commit
   → Report errors
   → Wait for user to fix or approve
```

---

## WHEN TO SKIP LOCAL VALIDATION

**Skip local validation ONLY when:**
- Committing from cloud agent (hook will run on server)
- User explicitly requests: `git commit --no-verify`
- Emergency hotfix (with explicit user approval)

**Otherwise, ALWAYS run local validation before committing.**

